{:edb/db-before-t 826 :edb/db-after-t 827 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534139 50 #inst "2026-10-06T04:19:31.185Z" 13194139534139 true] [17592186082954 1100 "The quadratic polynomial $P(x)$ has the double root $x_1=x_2=5$, and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1$. Find $P(x)$." 13194139534139 false] [17592186082954 1100 "The quadratic polynomial $P(x)$ has the double root $x_1=x_2=5,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1.$ Find $P(x).$" 13194139534139 true] [17592186082954 1145 "Since our quadratic polynomial has the double root\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}x_1=x_2=5}\n$$\n\nand the coefficient of the quadratic term is\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}a=1}\n$$\n\nwe can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na(x - x_{1})^{2} &= 1 \\cdot (x - 5)^{2} \\\\\n&= (x - 5)^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - 5)^{2} &= x^{2} - 10x + 25\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(x) = x^2 - 10x+25\n$$" 13194139534139 false] [17592186082954 1145 "Since our quadratic polynomial has the double root ${\\color{black}x_1=x_2=5},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is ${\\color{black}a=1},$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})^{2} & =1\\cdot {(x-5)}^{2} \\\\  & ={(x-5)}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x-5)}^{2} & ={x}^{2}-10x+25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x) = x^2 - 10x+25.$" 13194139534139 true] [17592186082955 1100 "The quadratic polynomial $f(z)$ with real coefficients has roots $z_1=3+\\textrm{i}$ and $z_2=3-\\textrm{i}$, and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $2$. Find $f(z)$." 13194139534139 false] [17592186082955 1100 "The quadratic polynomial $f(z)$ with real coefficients has roots $z_1=3+\\textrm{i}$ and $z_2=3-\\textrm{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $2.$ Find $f(z).$" 13194139534139 true] [17592186082955 1145 "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}z_1=3+\\textrm{i}}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}z_2=3-\\textrm{i}}\n$$\n\nand the coefficient of the quadratic term is\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}a=2}\n$$\n\nwe can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na(z - z_{1})(z - z_{2}) &= 2(z - (3 + \\textrm{i}))(z - (3 - \\textrm{i}))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(z - (3 + \\textrm{i}))(z - (3 - \\textrm{i})) &= 2(z^{2} - (3 + \\textrm{i})z - (3 - \\textrm{i})z + (3 + \\textrm{i})(3 - \\textrm{i})) \\\\\n&= 2(z^{2} - (3 + \\textrm{i} + 3 - \\textrm{i})z + (3^{2} - \\textrm{i}^{2})) \\\\\n&= 2(z^{2} - 6z + (9 + 1)) \\\\\n&= 2(z^{2} - 6z + 10) \\\\\n&= 2z^{2} - 12z + 20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf(z) = 2z^2-12z+20\n$$" 13194139534139 false] [17592186082955 1145 "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${\\color{black}z_1=3+\\textrm{i}}$ and ${\\color{black}z_2=3-\\textrm{i}},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is ${\\color{black}a=2},$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(z-{z}_{1})(z-{z}_{2}) & =2(z-(3+\\text{i}))(z-(3-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(z-(3+\\text{i}))(z-(3-\\text{i})) & =2({z}^{2}-(3+\\text{i})z-(3-\\text{i})z+(3+\\text{i})(3-\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2({z}^{2}-(3+\\text{i}+3-\\text{i})z+({3}^{2}-{\\text{i}}^{2})) \\\\  & =2({z}^{2}-6z+(9+1)) \\\\  & =2({z}^{2}-6z+10) \\\\  & =2{z}^{2}-12z+20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z) = 2z^2-12z+20.$" 13194139534139 true] [17592186082956 1100 "Factor $u^2-2u+10$." 13194139534139 false] [17592186082956 1100 "Factor $u^2-2u+10.$" 13194139534139 true] [17592186082956 1145 "First, we let\n\n$$\nf(u) = u^2-2u+10\n$$\n\nNext, we solve\n\n$$\nf(u) = 0\n$$\n\nby completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(u) &= 0 \\\\\nu^{2} - 2u + 10 &= 0 \\\\\n(u^{2} - 2u + 1^{2}) - 1^{2} + 10 &= 0 \\\\\n(u - 1)^{2} - 1 + 10 &= 0 \\\\\n(u - 1)^{2} + 9 &= 0 \\\\\n(u - 1)^{2} &= -9 \\\\\n(u - 1)^{2} &= 9\\textrm{i}^{2} \\\\\n(u - 1)^{2} &= (3\\textrm{i})^{2} \\\\\nu - 1 &= ± 3\\textrm{i} \\\\\nu &= 1 ± 3\\textrm{i}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since our quadratic equation has roots\n\n$$\nu_1=1+ 3\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nu_2=1- 3\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nand the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1$, the expression $u^2-2u+10$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu^{2} - 2u + 10 &= a(u - u_{1})(u - u_{2}) \\\\\n&= (u - (1 + 3\\textrm{i}))(u - (1 - 3\\textrm{i}))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534139 false] [17592186082956 1145 "First, we let $f(u) = u^2-2u+10.$\n\nNext, we solve $f(u) = 0$ by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(u) & =0 \\\\ {u}^{2}-2u+10 & =0 \\\\ ({u}^{2}-2u+{1}^{2})-{1}^{2}+10 & =0 \\\\ (u-1)^{2}-1+10 & =0 \\\\ (u-1)^{2}+9 & =0 \\\\ (u-1)^{2} & =-9 \\\\ (u-1)^{2} & =9{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ (u-1)^{2} & =(3\\text{i})^{2} \\\\ u-1 & =\\pm 3\\text{i} \\\\ u & =1\\pm 3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since our quadratic equation has roots $u_1=1+ 3\\textrm{i}$ and $u_2=1- 3\\textrm{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1,$ the expression $u^2-2u+10$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}-2u+10 & =a(u-{u}_{1})(u-{u}_{2}) \\\\  & =(u-(1+3\\text{i}))(u-(1-3\\text{i})).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534139 true] [17592186082961 1100 "The quadratic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_1=2, x_2=5$, and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $3$. Find $P(x)$." 13194139534139 false] [17592186082961 1100 "The quadratic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_1=2, x_2=5,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $3.$ Find $P(x).$" 13194139534139 true] [17592186082961 1145 "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}x_1=2}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}x_2=5}\n$$\n\nand the coefficient of the quadratic term is\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}a=3}\n$$\n\nwe can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na(x - x_{1})(x - x_{2}) &= 3(x - 2)(x - 5) \\\\\n&= 3(x - 2)(x - 5)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3(x - 2)(x - 5) &= 3(x^{2} - 7x + 10) \\\\\n&= 3x^{2} - 21x + 30\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(x) = 3x^2-21x+30\n$$" 13194139534139 false] [17592186082961 1145 "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${\\color{black}x_1=2}$ and ${\\color{black}x_2=5},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is ${\\color{black}a=3},$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}) & =3(x-2)(x-5) \\\\  & =3(x-2)(x-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x-2)(x-5) & =3({x}^{2}-7x+10) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}-21x+30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x) = 3x^2-21x+30.$" 13194139534139 true] [17592186083152 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278313 13194139534139 true] [17592186083152 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278327 13194139534139 true] [17592186083152 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278355 13194139534139 true] [17592186083152 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278359 13194139534139 true] [17592186083152 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278383 13194139534139 true] [17592186083153 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278345 13194139534139 true] [17592186083153 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278390 13194139534139 true] [17592186083153 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278397 13194139534139 true] [17592186083153 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278404 13194139534139 true] [17592186083154 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278320 13194139534139 true] [17592186083154 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278334 13194139534139 true] [17592186083154 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278362 13194139534139 true] [17592186083154 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278411 13194139534139 true] [17592186083154 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278418 13194139534139 true] [17592186083161 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278341 13194139534139 true] [17592186083161 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278352 13194139534139 true] [17592186083161 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278369 13194139534139 true] [17592186083161 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278376 13194139534139 true] [17592186083631 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534139 true] [17592186083631 1100 "The quadratic polynomial $P(t)$ has roots $t_{1} = 4, t_{2} = 3$, and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $2$. Find $P(t)$." 13194139534139 false] [17592186083631 1100 "The quadratic polynomial $P(t)$ has roots ${t}_{1}=4,{t}_{2}=3,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $2.$ Find $P(t).$" 13194139534139 true] [17592186083631 1145 "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${t}_{1}=4$ and ${t}_{2}=3,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t-{t}_{1})(t-{t}_{2}) & =(2)(t-4)(t-3) \\\\  & =2(t-4)(t-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(t-4)(t-3) & =2({t}^{2}-7t+12) \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}-14t+24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(t)=2{t}^{2}-14t+24.$" 13194139534139 true] [17592186083634 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534139 true] [17592186083634 1100 "The quadratic polynomial $f(z)$ has real coefficients, has roots $z_{1} = 4\\textrm{i}$ and $z_{2} =-4\\textrm{i}$, and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $-1$. Find $f(z)$." 13194139534139 false] [17592186083634 1100 "The quadratic polynomial $f(z)$ has real coefficients, has roots ${z}_{1}=4\\text{i}$ and ${z}_{2}=-4\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $-1.$ Find $f(z).$" 13194139534139 true] [17592186083634 1145 "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${z}_{1}=4\\text{i}$ and ${z}_{2}=-4\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=-1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(z-{z}_{1})(z-{z}_{2}) & =(-1)(z-4\\text{i})(z-(-4\\text{i})) \\\\  & =-(z-4\\text{i})(z+4\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(z-4\\text{i})(z+4\\text{i}) & =-({z}^{2}-(4\\text{i})^{2}) \\\\  & =-({z}^{2}-16{\\text{i}}^{2}) \\\\  & =-({z}^{2}+16) \\\\  & =-{z}^{2}-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=-{z}^{2}-16.$" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278313 1017 #edb/ref 17592186278314 13194139534139 true] [17592186278313 1089 "q-104330" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278313 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534139 true] [17592186278313 1100 "The quadratic polynomial $P(x)$ has the double root ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{3},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=9.$ Find $P(x).$" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278313 1113 #uuid "6d0aac9d-6cc7-5552-8099-d9c726cdd252" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278313 1145 "Since our quadratic polynomial has the double root ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{3},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=9,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})^{2} & =9{(x-(-\\frac{2}{3}))}^{2} \\\\  & =9{(x+\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{(x+\\frac{2}{3})}^{2} & =9({x}^{2}+\\frac{4}{3}x+\\frac{4}{9}) \\\\  & =9{x}^{2}+12x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=9{x}^{2}+12x+4.$" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278314 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278315 13194139534139 true] [17592186278314 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278316 13194139534139 true] [17592186278314 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278317 13194139534139 true] [17592186278314 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278318 13194139534139 true] [17592186278314 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278319 13194139534139 true] [17592186278314 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534139 true] [17592186278314 1041 "selection" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278314 1104 #edb/ref 17592186278317 13194139534139 true] [17592186278314 1110 #uuid "085411cc-4f1c-5e5d-8088-6aa979d52a91" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278315 1034 "9{x}^{2}+6x-12" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278315 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534139 true] [17592186278315 1111 #uuid "9c7799e0-c38a-59d5-81c8-48db76d084c1" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278316 1034 "9{x}^{2}-6x+6" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278316 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534139 true] [17592186278316 1111 #uuid "02199bf7-9e3a-5585-bf0f-0ea9df1c6c30" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278317 1034 "9{x}^{2}+12x+4" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278317 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534139 true] [17592186278317 1111 #uuid "4a7854b8-c2cb-5989-9dec-46d0258bf5f8" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278318 1034 "9{x}^{2}-12x+4" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278318 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534139 true] [17592186278318 1111 #uuid "73b95c43-24d8-5889-be62-9f7d0626ca8f" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278319 1034 "9{x}^{2}-6x-4" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278319 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534139 true] [17592186278319 1111 #uuid "eed7dfcf-ebac-554a-ad89-ab7a2456b953" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278320 1017 #edb/ref 17592186278321 13194139534139 true] [17592186278320 1089 "q-107523" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278320 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534139 true] [17592186278320 1100 "Which of the following is a factor of ${u}^{2}-2u+5?$" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278320 1113 #uuid "54ac6bbc-3ef6-59e6-9f7d-2343e7a4c075" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278320 1145 "First, we let $f(u)={u}^{2}-2u+5.$\n\nNext, we solve $f(u)=0$ by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(u) & =0 \\\\ {u}^{2}-2u+5 & =0 \\\\ ({u}^{2}-2\\cdot u+{1}^{2})-{1}^{2}+5 & =0 \\\\ (u-1)^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ (u-1)^{2} & =-4 \\\\ (u-1)^{2} & =4{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ (u-1)^{2} & =(2\\text{i})^{2} \\\\ u-1 & =\\pm 2\\text{i} \\\\ u & =1\\pm 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince our quadratic equation has roots ${u}_{1}=1+2\\text{i}$ and ${u}_{2}=1-2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1,$ the expression ${u}^{2}-2u+5$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}-2u+5 & =a(u-{u}_{1})(u-{u}_{2}) \\\\  & =(u-(1+2\\text{i}))(u-(1-2\\text{i})).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, among the given options, only $u-(1-2\\text{i})$ is a factor of ${u}^{2}-2u+5.$" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278321 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278322 13194139534139 true] [17592186278321 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278323 131941395