-3{x}^{2}-9x+30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-3{x}^{2}-9x+30.$" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278342 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278343 13194139534139 true] [17592186278342 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278344 13194139534139 true] [17592186278342 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534139 true] [17592186278342 1041 "field-1" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278342 1104 #edb/ref 17592186278344 13194139534139 true] [17592186278342 1110 #uuid "bfec8835-f216-5930-b0de-838ed3570de5" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278343 1034 "-3x^2+9x+30" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278343 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534139 true] [17592186278343 1111 #uuid "d513065d-9c14-5425-aeea-3995ee21b69d" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278344 1034 "-3x^2-9x+30" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278344 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534139 true] [17592186278344 1111 #uuid "e3175648-7718-5eeb-a2a8-de33dc893e58" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278345 1017 #edb/ref 17592186278346 13194139534139 true] [17592186278345 1089 "q-28185" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278345 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534139 true] [17592186278345 1100 "The quadratic polynomial $f(x)$ has real coefficients, has roots ${x}_{1}=6\\text{i}$ and ${x}_{2}=-6\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $1.$ Find $f(x).$" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278345 1113 #uuid "847b083e-81ae-5df7-a482-aef291b5630a" 13194139534139 true] [17592186278345 1145 "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=6\\text{i}$ and ${x}_{2}=-6\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}) & =(1)(x-6\\text{i})(x-(-6\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(x-6\\text{i})(x+6\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-6\\text{i})(x+6\\text{i}) & ={x}^{2}-(6\\text{i})^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-36{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)={x}^{2}+36.$" 13194139534139 true] 